@startuml tool-admission
title Tool admission - accepted option B / proposed record grammar; D-PATH decided; option C deferred
actor "Operator\nsystem/fleet policy authority" as O
participant "Curator manager\noperator UID; resolver/provisioner" as M
participant "Enabled signed tool registries\neach registry operator owns dedicated rotating keys" as R
database "Manager-owned protected state\ntrust bundle/config, URL high-water\nlocks, sealed store, launch alias directory" as S
participant "Caller-side curator-run + agents-management\ncaller UID; sole semantic composer" as L
participant "Destination executor\nadmitted execution UID bound by plan\nagent-account curator-run for broker; SH2 runner later" as E
participant "Harness or declared script worker\nchild identity from admitted plan" as H
O -> S: configure registry order, pinned key sets/freshness; separate release trust bundle
note over O,S: No compiled-in trust keys. Publisher/service and bundle delivery unspecified in spec CIP-0007 Open questions.
O -> M: install/resolve/refresh or lock replay
M -> M: read logical dependency id / alias / constraint / platform as untrusted data
M -> M: admit declaration: no author URL/checksum/signature; deny override wins (proposed)
break invalid identity, alias/version collision or policy denial
  M --> O: structured refusal; no fetch from author or fallback
end
M -> R: phase 1: scan every enabled trusted registry for candidate revocations
R --> M: signed snapshots/records/revocations
M -> S: verify current keys/freshness and persisted URL rollback high-water
note right of M: Malformed/unmatched/unverifiable records ignored with warning; not trusted permits.
break unreachable trusted registry / incomplete revocation evidence / rollback or authorization failure
  M --> O: fail closed; name affected registry/tools; no availability-preferring B mode
end
alt verified revocation in any enabled registry covers artifact or record
  M --> O: veto before positive selection; allow override cannot waive it
else no verified matching revocation after full scan
  alt replay existing lock
    M -> S: exact locked version/platform/hash/registry; recheck current authorization
    break removed signing key, stale record or no longer authorized artifact
      M --> O: refuse replay even when store bytes/hash exist
    end
  else resolve / explicit refresh
    M -> R: phase 2: first configured layer with verified non-revoked satisfying record
    R --> M: exact selected version/platform URL, format, map, hash
    M -> M: highest satisfying version; refresh never downgrades without explicit approval (proposed)
    break unknown/unsigned identity or no satisfying verified record
      M --> O: refuse; add trusted registry; no C mirror/system probe fallback
    end
  end
  M -> M: provision manager-owned sealed files; verify exact artifact bytes
  M -> S: record exact lock and store identity; expose provisioned alias in protected launch bin
  note right of S: Store/publication failure recovery details unspecified in spec CIP-0007; no invented transaction order.
  M -> L: protected tool directory + admitted command context
  L -> E: immutable composed plan; destination applies its admitted typed transform
  E -> E: after destination child-environment admission: tools first, base order, dispatcher
  note right of E
    Deduplicate by identity; preserve existing dispatcher position, otherwise append.
    Bind resolved PATH/context into immutable plan digest; repository .agents/bin excluded.
  end note
  alt PATH absent/excluded or admission malformed/unreadable
    E --> O: refuse command capability; never recreate excluded PATH
  else managed harness launch
    E -> H: exact provisioned aliases by accepted launch exposure; no system-wide install
  else enforced script-worker-v1
    E -> H: only resolved interpreter + declared exec names; discard inherited PATH
    note right of H: Tool dependency never widens enforced PATH; alias must also be declared exec.
  end
end
note over M,E
  Option B has no PATH version probes or system-tool reuse; those remain option C.
  [[../CIP-0007-manager-provisioned-cli-tools.md#operator-decision-2026-10-10 CIP-0007 acceptance conditions]]
  [[../CIP-0007-manager-provisioned-cli-tools.md#recommendation CIP-0007 scan/selection/replay]]
  [[../CIP-0007-manager-provisioned-cli-tools.md#security-considerations CIP-0007 authorization/keys]]
  [[../platform-contract-disposition.md#managed-and-interactive-path D-PATH]]
end note
@enduml
